# 11. DARK/LIGHT MODE FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

Theme switching is a core feature.

Requirements:

1. Provide a theme toggle in the global navigation.
2. Support dark and light themes.
3. Use dark mode as the initial fallback.
4. Respect the system preference on the first visit when possible.
5. Allow manual theme selection.
6. Store the manually selected preference in localStorage.
7. Restore the selected theme after refresh.
8. Maintain theme consistency across all routes.
9. Provide a smooth transition.
10. Use accessible labels for the toggle.
11. Avoid a visible flash of the wrong theme during initial loading.

All colors must use centralized design tokens or CSS variables.

