# 16. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

## 16.1 Performance

- Optimize images.
- Lazy-load below-the-fold images.
- Avoid unnecessarily large JavaScript bundles.
- Limit excessive animation.
- Use efficient rendering.
- Minimize layout shifts.
- Use appropriate caching.

Performance goals:

- Largest Contentful Paint: 2.5 seconds or less.
- Interaction to Next Paint: 200 milliseconds or less.
- Cumulative Layout Shift: 0.1 or less.

These should be targeted at the 75th percentile for real-user data where available.

## 16.2 Responsiveness

The website must work across:

- Mobile phones.
- Tablets.
- Laptops.
- Desktop monitors.
- Large displays.

No horizontal overflow should occur.

## 16.3 Accessibility

Target WCAG 2.2 AA practices.

Requirements:
- Semantic HTML.
- Keyboard navigation.
- Visible focus indicators.
- Accessible form labels.
- Meaningful image alt text.
- Proper color contrast.
- Screen-reader-friendly controls.
- Reduced-motion support.

## 16.4 Security

- Validate form data on the server.
- Sanitize user input.
- Protect API credentials.
- Use HTTPS.
- Implement rate limiting.
- Prevent spam submissions.
- Avoid exposing sensitive server information.
- Do not commit environment secrets to GitHub.

## 16.5 SEO

- Unique page titles.
- Meta descriptions.
- Open Graph metadata.
- Descriptive URLs.
- Sitemap.
- Robots.txt.
- Canonical URLs where appropriate.
- Appropriate heading hierarchy.
- Descriptive image alt text.
- Relevant structured data where justified.

## 16.6 Browser Compatibility

Support modern versions of:

- Google Chrome.
- Microsoft Edge.
- Mozilla Firefox.
- Safari.

